{
  "_readme": [
    "Mbali's seed for 2026: her own data only. Each key is a table and each row uses the table's column names.",
    "Her plans point into the approved 2026 rules, which only sage load writes, from data/rules/2026/rulebook.json. sage seed and sage sign-in refuse until they're loaded.",
    "Rows carry no uuids or student_id. sage seed fills student_id from the signed-in account and makes the uuids.",
    "fake_account holds Mbali's made-up email: the tests' fake sign-in uses it, and sage sign-in makes her local account from it. sage seed never writes it: a real account brings its own email.",
    "Rows that point at other seed rows use local keys: plan_set, plan, other_plan, chat, open_plan. sage seed swaps them for uuids.",
    "chats.plan and other_plan must be stored with plan_id < other_plan_id, so sage seed orders each pair after making the uuids.",
    "course_history is my own 2023-2025 record, used for Mbali by my choice. The planner prototype already shows it.",
    "course_history keeps the codes her record prints, such as EEE1006F. The approved 2026 equivalences say which 2026 courses they count as.",
    "plan_sets.answers holds the questionnaire's answers as {question id: option id}. Wanting EEE4119F with no week preference keeps exactly the 7 plans left visible."
  ],
